From 1735e0af3c1858ab49a830d14b4e9c18de870027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:07:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] =?UTF-8?q?feat(annotate):=20a=20text=20box=20is=20tex?=
 =?UTF-8?q?t=20=E2=80=94=20on=20the=20page,=20edited=20there,=20and=20undo?=
 =?UTF-8?q?able?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reported as "the text box is bold, doesn't show the text at all", and that is
exactly what it was. A text annotation drew an empty rectangle with a 2 pt
frame in the highlighter's yellow, and put its words in a 10 px badge floating
above the box, truncated at 24 characters. The text itself was only editable in
a textarea in the far right sidebar. Nothing about that says "text box".

Now the words are drawn inside their own rectangle, in the annotation's colour,
at its point size converted against the page's real width in points — so what
is on screen is what will be in the file. The caret lands in the box the moment
it is drawn, and a double-click puts it back. Typing commits on blur, not per
keystroke, so one undo takes back a sentence rather than a letter. An empty box
is removed instead of being left on the page as an invisible rectangle.

The colour and opacity are now held per tool family — highlighter yellow at 70%
for markup, ink at 100% for everything else — each remembering what the user
last chose for it. One shared swatch is how a text box came to be drawn in
#facc15. The line-width slider is gone for text, where it only ever produced
that frame, and a text box is created with no border at all.

And undo, which did not exist anywhere. Markup is batched locally until Save,
so the local stores are exactly what a person can undo: a snapshot per gesture,
Undo/Redo in the page bar, ⌘Z and ⇧⌘Z, skipped while a field has focus so the
browser's own undo wins inside the editor.

Verified end to end against the live API: draw, type, save, download — the
downloaded file carries a /FreeText annotation with the text, in 0.2 0.176
0.141 rg at 12 pt.

Design contract §3 gains "Text on the page"; §4 records Annotate's undo.

