From 161758b809fbf42f6c12089b0d92096ce9deb713 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:07:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(workspace): the viewer that never loaded, and a
 screen that never fitted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four things, all of them why the workspace looked broken.

**The viewer never started in production.** ngx-extended-pdf-viewer feature-
detects the browser by injecting an inline `<script>`, and our CSP is
`script-src 'self'` — so it was refused, the viewer never initialised, and
`/api/documents/{id}/content/` was never requested at all. Blank pane, no
console error anyone had noticed. The library ships an external
`op-chaining-support.js` for exactly this case; `[useInlineScripts]="false"`
takes it. And behind that, nginx served pdf.js's own `.mjs` modules as
`application/octet-stream` — stock `mime.types` knows neither `.mjs` nor
`.wasm` — which `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` (rightly) makes fatal for a
module script. Both configs pin the type now.

**The workspace never filled the screen.** Its host is a flex item of the
shell's `main` and was not saying so, so a child asking for `h-full` inside a
host with `height: auto` was circular: on a 900 px screen the reading pane came
out 318 px tall with 400 px of empty backdrop under it, in every mode.

**On a phone it was unusable.** A 390 px viewport cannot hold a 208 px rail, a
page and a 256 px rail; nothing said so, so the row overflowed, the page grew
with it and the mode nav — View, Organize, Edit, Annotate — sat off the right
edge with no way to reach it. The panes stack below `md` (`.ws-panes` /
`.ws-rail` / `.ws-pane-main`), the bar scrolls inside itself, and the annotate
page seeds its width from the viewport instead of a fixed 900.

**And the failure screens had no header at all.** The shell hides its own
header inside `/app/doc/:id` and the loading and error branches have no
workspace bar, so a stranded visitor got a sentence in the middle of nothing —
no brand, no theme toggle, no way out. They carry a minimal bar now. A throttle
is no longer dressed as a breakage either: it says what it is and holds the
retry button for the number of seconds the server asked for.

Two smaller things while in here: an Undo in the workspace bar, which is the
version-level revert that was previously buried three clicks deep in the
History tab; and file sizes in the unit that says something — a 40 KB page and
an empty file both read "0.0 MB".

Design contract §3 gains the pane spec and amends the workspace-bar and
loading/error entries; §4 records the height rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y58KHCbQzb6yAzQv9a6xbQ
