From d197c59f1a68160b9cae8891a0f96d3e30771828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(tools): merge in the order the visitor added the
 files
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`/merge-pdf` tells the visitor on its own page that "page order follows the
order you add the files", and then did not do that. The uploads run
concurrently and each result was recorded with `push`, so `document_ids` went
out in the order the *network* finished — and `tasks.py` merges strictly
positionally. Add a 20 MB chapter and then a 200 KB cover and the cover merged
second, differently on a different connection. `/compare-pdf` shares the call
and can invert the diff the same way.

A slot per file, filled at the file's own index. The test gates the two uploads
so the second finishes first, which is the case that was silently wrong.

Recorded as known-not-fixed on 2026-08-19; it is a one-line ordering bug in a
headline tool, so it is fixed here rather than carried further.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y58KHCbQzb6yAzQv9a6xbQ
