+| 2026-08-10 | **Production workspace viewer never loads the document.** `/app/doc/<id>` as a guest in desktop Chrome: metadata, versions, outline and all thumbnails answer 200, **no `.../content/` request is ever made**, the pdf.js canvas stays blank and the console stays silent — reproduced across SPA navigation and a hard reload. Tool-page funnel (upload -> result -> download) unaffected. This is the 2026-08-02 "nothing asserts a page drew" row, live in production. Chase: H3 local gate, then H2 `@smoke` vs production (`docs/ops/railway-handoff-claude-cli.md`); whichever way it falls, add the page-actually-drew assertion so it cannot return. | 1/10 | No | ✔ **Root-caused and fixed 2026-08-20** — two blockers, both production-only, which is why the console stayed silent locally. (a) ngx-extended-pdf-viewer feature-detects the browser by injecting an **inline `<script>`**; `script-src 'self'` refuses it, so the viewer never initialised and therefore never asked for the document. `[useInlineScripts]="false"` takes the library's own external `op-chaining-support.js` instead. (b) nginx served pdf.js's `.mjs` modules as `application/octet-stream` (stock `mime.types` knows neither `.mjs` nor `.wasm`), which `nosniff` makes fatal for a module script — both configs pin the type now. Verified in a production-faithful harness: `viewer-*.min.mjs`, `pdf.worker-*.min.mjs` and `/api/documents/{id}/content/` all 200 and the page draws. **The page-actually-drew assertion is still owed** — see the new row below. |
